While developing the connector, please fill out this form. This information is needed to write docs and to help other users set up the connector.

## Connector capabilities

1. What resources does the connector sync?

    -Users
    -Folders
    -Documents

2. Can the connector provision any resources? If so, which ones?

    Yes, folders, documents and accounts

    Accounts can also be deprovisioned (deleted). Delete goes through Lucid's SCIM
    surface, so it requires the SCIM token listed under "Connector credentials" and
    is only available on Enterprise accounts.

3. Does the connector support any actions? If so, which ones?

    Yes, three account actions. All three run against Lucid's SCIM surface, so all
    three require the SCIM token and are Enterprise-only:

    -`enable_user` — reactivates an account (SCIM active=true)
    -`disable_user` — deactivates an account (SCIM active=false); soft and reversible
    -`update_user` — updates an account's firstName, lastName, email, username or roles

    Note on roles: account creation (REST POST /v1/users) and update_user (SCIM
    PATCH /Users/{id}) take different role spellings. update_user accepts either the
    SCIM names (AccountAdmin, BillingAdmin, Developer, DocumentAdmin,
    EnterpriseShieldAdmin, TemplateAdmin) or the kebab-case creation names
    (team-admin, billing-admin, developer, document-admin, enterprise-shield-admin,
    template-admin), translating the latter for you. The four remaining creation-time
    roles — account-owner, group-admin, organizational-group-admin and team-manager —
    have no SCIM equivalent and cannot be changed after the account exists.

## Connector credentials

1. What credentials or information are needed to set up the connector? (For example, API key, client ID and secret, domain, etc.)

    -API Key
    -OAuth 2 credentials (client-id and client-secret)
    -SCIM bearer token, "SCIM for admin management" (Enterprise only; optional, but required for user delete and the enable/disable/update-profile actions)
    -SCIM bearer token, "SCIM for content access" (Enterprise only; optional — Lucid's second SCIM integration)

2. For each item in the list above: 

   * How does a user create or look up that credential or info? Please include links to (non-gated) documentation, screenshots (of the UI or of gated docs), or a video of the process. 

       In the Lucidchart developer portal, navigate to API Keys.

    Click + Create API Key.

    Give the new key a name, such as “ConductorOne” and set an expiration, if desired.

    Give the key the following grants:
        Documents - Edit
        Folders - Edit

    Click Generate API key. The new key is created.

    Carefully copy and save the API key.

    OAuth 2: https://developer.lucid.co/docs/oauth-20-client-creation 

    For creating Users: https://lucid.readme.io/reference/createuser
    Use of this endpoint can only be authorized by administrators on accounts with Enterprise licenses.
    OAuth 2.0 Account Token Scopes: account.user

    SCIM token: in the Lucid admin panel, go to Admin > App Integration > SCIM and
    generate a bearer token. The same page shows the SCIM base URL
    (https://users.lucid.app/scim/v2). Only account admins can reach this page, and it
    is in the admin panel only — not the developer portal. SCIM is Enterprise-only and
    must be enabled for the account by Lucid support.
    SCIM reference: https://lucid.readme.io/reference/overview-scim

    Pass the token with the --lucid-scim-token flag or the BATON_LUCID_SCIM_TOKEN
    environment variable. Without it, sync, folder/document provisioning and account
    creation all still work, but account delete and the
    enable_user/disable_user/update_user actions return Unimplemented.

    SCIM tokens: https://developer.lucid.co/reference/overview-scim
    Lucid ships two separate SCIM integrations, and both are served from the SAME base URL,
    https://users.lucid.app/scim/v2. Nothing in the URL distinguishes them — the bearer token
    alone determines which integration a call reaches, so each one has its own token:
        • "SCIM for admin management" — syncs to organizational groups. This is the
          lucid-scim-token setting, and it is what gates user delete and the
          enable_user / disable_user / update_user actions.
        • "SCIM for content access" — syncs to teams. This is the lucid-content-access-scim-token
          setting. It is optional and additive: when configured, deleting a user also
          deprovisions them from this integration.
    Both are Enterprise-tier features; generate each token in the Lucid admin panel under the
    corresponding SCIM integration.

