## Optional connector flags

* `--lucid-scim-token` (string, default: empty)

    SCIM 2.0 bearer token, described under "Connector credentials" above. Enables account delete and the `enable_user` / `disable_user` / `update_user` actions. Enterprise-only. Without it those operations return `Unimplemented`; everything else works.

* `--lucid-content-access-scim-token` (string, secret, no default)

    The bearer token for Lucid's second SCIM integration, **"SCIM for content access"**, which syncs to teams. It is separate from `--lucid-scim-token` (the "SCIM for admin management" integration, which syncs to organizational groups); both integrations share the same base URL and are told apart only by the token.

    Optional and additive: it extends delete rather than replacing `--lucid-scim-token`. When it is set, deleting a user removes them from admin management first and from content access second. If the first succeeds and the second fails, the connector returns a partial-deprovisioning error naming both halves instead of reporting success, so a user who may still hold team content access never looks like a completed offboarding.

* `--scim-base-url` (string, default: `https://users.lucid.app/scim/v2`)

    The Lucid SCIM 2.0 base URL, used by both SCIM tokens. Leave it empty on commercial accounts — the default is correct.

    FedRAMP/GovSuite tenants must set it. Lucid publishes no fixed FedRAMP SCIM hostname: unlike the REST API, which swaps `api.lucid.co` for `api.lucidgov.app`, the SCIM base URL for a GovSuite account is generated per account inside the customer's own GovSuite admin panel, so the connector cannot derive it.

* `--lucid-content-transfer-user-email` (string, default: empty)

    Email address of the user who should receive a deleted user's owned documents. When set, a delete calls `POST /v1/transferUserContent` first so the content is retained rather than removed with the account. Must be an email address, not a user ID — the Lucid API requires email. The OAuth token needs the `account.user.transfercontent` scope; without it the transfer call returns 403.

* `--exclude-shortcuts` (boolean, default: `false`)

    By default, the connector **also synchronizes documents and folders that are shortcuts** (`isShortcut=true`). If you prefer to skip them (because they don't grant effective permissions or might return 403/404 errors from the API), run the connector with the `--exclude-shortcuts` flag or set the configuration parameter `exclude-shortcuts: true` in the connector definition.